"rather"}, {"start": 225.96, "end": 226.14, "text": "than"}, {"start": 226.14, "end": 226.24, "text": "a"}, {"start": 226.24, "end": 226.44, "text": "world"}, {"start": 226.44, "end": 226.76, "text": "of"}, {"start": 226.76, "end": 227.1, "text": "eyesight,"}, {"start": 227.7, "end": 227.88, "text": "like"}, {"start": 227.88, "end": 228.14, "text": "our"}, {"start": 228.14, "end": 228.4, "text": "brain"}, {"start": 228.4, "end": 228.54, "text": "is"}, {"start": 228.54, "end": 229.04, "text": "constructed,"}, {"start": 229.44, "end": 229.56, "text": "and"}, {"start": 229.56, "end": 229.78, "text": "most"}, {"start": 229.78, "end": 230.4, "text": "important."}, {"start": 230.86, "end": 231.14, "text": "They"}, {"start": 231.14, "end": 231.36, "text": "may"}, {"start": 231.36, "end": 231.56, "text": "be"}, {"start": 231.56, "end": 231.72, "text": "able"}, {"start": 231.72, "end": 231.88, "text": "to"}, {"start": 231.88, "end": 232.06, "text": "see"}, {"start": 232.06, "end": 232.16, "text": "see"}, {"start": 232.16, "end": 232.24, "text": "the"}, {"start": 232.24, "end": 232.68, "text": "outcome"}, {"start": 232.68, "end": 232.96, "text": "of"}, {"start": 232.96, "end": 233.3, "text": "future"}, {"start": 233.3, "end": 233.82, "text": "events"}, {"start": 233.82, "end": 234.76, "text": "much"}, {"start": 234.76, "end": 235.22, "text": "better"}, {"start": 235.22, "end": 235.42, "text": "than"}, {"start": 235.42, "end": 235.8, "text": "us."}, {"start": 235.8, "end": 236.56, "text": "They'll"}, {"start": 236.56, "end": 236.68, "text": "be"}, {"start": 236.68, "end": 237.06, "text": "able"}, {"start": 237.06, "end": 237.26, "text": "to"}, {"start": 237.26, "end": 237.74, "text": "actually"}, {"start": 237.74, "end": 238.68, "text": "run"}, {"start": 238.68, "end": 239.34, "text": "circles"}, {"start": 239.34, "end": 239.68, "text": "around"}, {"start": 239.68, "end": 240.08, "text": "us"}, {"start": 240.08, "end": 240.72, "text": "because"}, {"start": 240.72, "end": 241.02, "text": "they"}, {"start": 241.02, "end": 241.48, "text": "see"}, {"start": 241.48, "end": 242.06, "text": "the"}, {"start": 242.06, "end": 242.56, "text": "future."}], "segments": [{"start": 0.0, "end": 3.52, "text": "I love to watch science fiction movies, but I cringe."}, {"start": 4.06, "end": 7.0, "text": "I cringe whenever I see a depiction of the aliens."}, {"start": 7.76, "end": 9.8, "text": "First of all, the aliens speak perfect English."}, {"start": 10.34, "end": 13.68, "text": "Not just British English, they speak perfect American English."}, {"start": 14.42, "end": 18.38, "text": "And obviously, they're a human inside some kind of monkey suit."}, {"start": 19.26, "end": 21.22, "text": "I mean, we have Hollywood special effects, right?"}, {"start": 21.3, "end": 23.12, "text": "So why can't we get better aliens?"}, {"start": 23.62, "end": 27.2, "text": "And then the aliens think just like us."}, {"start": 27.66, "end": 28.64, "text": "They're territorial."}, {"start": 28.64, "end": 35.56, "text": "They want to conquer. They want resources. They want, they see humans as inferior."}, {"start": 36.04, "end": 39.44, "text": "But you see, that's only a byproduct of our evolution."}, {"start": 40.04, "end": 44.4, "text": "Look at other animals in the animal kingdom. Some animals are not territorial."}, {"start": 45.24, "end": 50.58, "text": "They don't have to conquer. We have other paradigms in the animal kingdom"}, {"start": 50.58, "end": 54.18, "text": "which are totally different from the way our brain is constructed."}, {"start": 54.18, "end": 60.54, "text": "But when we look at aliens in the movies, we're basically projecting our own consciousness"}, {"start": 61.21, "end": 68.48, "text": "in aliens, our fears, our desires, our projected, and they are a mirror of who we are, not"}, {"start": 68.48, "end": 70.58, "text": "a mirror of who they really are."}, {"start": 71.02, "end": 78.32, "text": "For example, if you take a look at a bat or a dog, the dog's brain is mainly interested"}, {"start": 78.32, "end": 86.04, "text": "in smells. It's swirling in a universe of smells, while a bass brain may be concentrated"}, {"start": 86.04, "end": 93.14, "text": "on sonar, on detecting clicks and echoes. Same thing with the dolphin brain. Their consciousness"}, {"start": 93.14, "end": 98.82, "text": "is totally different from our consciousness because they see things differently than us"}, {"start": 98.82, "end": 104.86, "text": "because of their evolutionary history. For example, when we see a cat and the cat comes"}, {"start": 104.86, "end": 111.54, "text": "up to us and prostrate per next to us. We say to ourselves, oh, nice cat. Cat is being"}, {"start": 111.54, "end": 118.1, "text": "affectionate. No. The cat is not being affectionate. It's simply rubbing his hormones on you and"}, {"start": 118.1, "end": 126.06, "text": "saying, I own this human. This human is mine. I'm marking my territory. This human feeds"}, {"start": 126.06, "end": 133.02, "text": "me twice a day. I've trained him. So a cat sees the universe totally different than we do and"}, {"start": 133.02, "end": 135.58, "text": "and yet we impose our thinking on an alien."}, {"start": 136.24, "end": 137.7, "text": "Now on the question of intelligence,"}, {"start": 138.62, "end": 141.0, "text": "if these aliens are more intelligent than us,"}, {"start": 141.36, "end": 142.84, "text": "how would they be more intelligent?"}, {"start": 143.52, "end": 145.82, "text": "In the book, I say that one of the main ingredients"}, {"start": 145.82, "end": 148.82, "text": "of intelligence is to predict the future."}, {"start": 149.52, "end": 153.32, "text": "The ability to simulate today, so we see tomorrow."}, {"start": 153.98, "end": 156.28, "text": "And that requires a high level of intelligence"}, {"start": 156.72, "end": 159.16, "text": "to be able to understand the laws of nature,"}, {"start": 159.34, "end": 162.56, "text": "the laws of people, what is the most likely outcome"}, {"start": 162.56, "end": 169.24, "text": "of a future event. That requires intelligence. If they are more intelligent than us, they"}, {"start": 169.24, "end": 175.64, "text": "will see the future much better than us. They will see outcomes that we cannot foresee."}, {"start": 176.18, "end": 182.04, "text": "They will simulate scenarios that we cannot even dream of. They can outweigh us every"}, {"start": 182.04, "end": 189.72, "text": "time. Think of a safe cracker. A safe cracker may have a low IQ, may have dropped out of"}, {"start": 189.72, "end": 196.62, "text": "elementary school, but the safe cracker can simulate the future much better than a"}, {"start": 196.62, "end": 200.48, "text": "cop can, and that's why he can rob banks and get away with it."}, {"start": 201.16, "end": 207.34, "text": "In other words, the criminal mind is not necessarily stupid because it has low IQ, it's quite"}, {"start": 207.34, "end": 212.92, "text": "well adapted for what it does, and what it does is to simulate the future of a crime."}, {"start": 212.92, "end": 219.54, "text": "Now, think about when we encounter intelligent life that is more intelligent than us."}, {"start": 220.02, "end": 221.94, "text": "They may see the world totally differently."}, {"start": 222.44, "end": 227.1, "text": "The world may be a world of smells, a world of sounds, rather than a world of eyesight,"}, {"start": 227.7, "end": 230.4, "text": "like our brain is constructed, and most important."}, {"start": 230.86, "end": 232.06, "text": "They may be able to see"}, {"start": 232.06, "end": 235.8, "text": "see the outcome of future events much better than us."}, {"start": 235.8, "end": 242.56, "text": "They'll be able to actually run circles around us because they see the future."}]}